# Build context for backend/Dockerfile and frontend/Dockerfile, which both
# build from the repo root.
#
# node_modules is the entry that matters. With no ignore file, the frontend's
# `COPY frontend ./frontend` laid the host's pnpm symlink farm over the one the
# image had just installed. Those links name the exact versions the host last
# resolved, so the moment the lockfile moved ahead of the host's last install
# the image lost the build tool outright — reported as a missing module, which
# points at the package rather than at the stale directory that shadowed it.
**/node_modules
**/.venv

.git
.github
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
**/.pytest_cache
**/.ruff_cache
**/.mypy_cache

# Rebuilt inside the image; a stale host copy would be served instead.
frontend/dist
**/*.tsbuildinfo

# Agent scratch space and local editor state, never part of an image.
.agents
.claude
**/.DS_Store
